#: ../../source/docs/common-simple-object-avoidance.rst:6
#: 6c16c32b76f94f548005eb16b84e5a2c
msgid "Simple Object Avoidance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-simple-object-avoidance.rst:8
#: de10976aab8c4d6b995eea8b8dbd624e
msgid "Copter supports simple object avoidance horizontally and upward, while Rover avoids simple objects by only stopping. Both use proximity sensors such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-simple-object-avoidance.rst:10
#: cd26cd870950418ba3fd5915f98bbd89
msgid "360 degree lidar including the :ref:`Lightware SF40C <copter:common-lightware-sf40c-objectavoidance>`, :ref:`TeraRanger Tower <copter:common-teraranger-tower-objectavoidance>` or :ref:`RPLidarA2/A3 <copter:common-rplidar-a2>`. See the :ref:`Proximity Sensor page<common-proximity-landingpage>` for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-simple-object-avoidance.rst:11
#: 80dcd70354904361aa495fc88916926d
msgid "Any of the supported :ref:`Rangefinders <common-rangefinder-landingpage>`. Up to 9 rangefinders can be used for object avoidance. See :ref:`common-rangefinder-setup` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-simple-object-avoidance.rst:12
#: f407bd71837241beb3e3728169b87ec6
msgid "Sensors capable of providing `MAVLink Distance Sensor <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#DISTANCE_SENSOR>`__ messages (like `OpenKai with a 3D camera <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qk_hEtRASqg>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-simple-object-avoidance.rst:13
#: 505fb488bbe0475a8f9101cc4bfaa4fd
msgid "3D Obstacle Avoidance via the new Mavlink message `OBSTACLE_DISTANCE_3D <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/ardupilotmega.html#OBSTACLE_DISTANCE_3D>`__ . Depth cameras can use this message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-simple-object-avoidance.rst:20
#: d885b36fc1014e119e2dc130998562cd
msgid "In addition, Simple Object Avoidance can use Geo-Fences and Fence Beacons as proximity sensors as determined by the setting of the :ref:`AVOID_ENABLE<AVOID_ENABLE>` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-simple-object-avoidance.rst:24
#: 210cbccb093344b18834d5ff5b8c87aa
msgid "Simple Object Avoidance Algorithms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-simple-object-avoidance.rst:26
#: a98bac8159e84722ac26eb3ed796a645
msgid "Horizontal object avoidance works in :ref:`AltHold <altholdmode>` and :ref:`Loiter <loiter-mode>` modes.  Upward object avoidance works in LOITER, ALTHOLD modes only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-simple-object-avoidance.rst:28
#: 09e055473c584ca68a5d619a618f9d7d
msgid "Only one proximity sensor source can be enabled, using either a 360 degree lidar or up to 9 rangefinders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-simple-object-avoidance.rst:30
#: aae6aacc17fd48429cfca80eb9dc0c84
msgid "For Object Avoidance in AUTO and GUIDED modes in Copter and Rover, see :ref:`common-oa-bendyruler` or :ref:`common-oa-dijkstras`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-simple-object-avoidance.rst:32
#: 993362cfe43f4a40b2f4a05940579dbb
msgid "Details on how simple object avoidance is implemented for Copter in ALTHOLD and LOITER mode can be found :ref:`here in the developer wiki <dev:code-overview-object-avoidance>` and involves assessing all the objects detected, in all reported quadrants, and adds control input to the pilot's,trying to move away from the aggregate threat or stop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-simple-object-avoidance.rst:34
#: 6772c056ecaa46f2a72919169e58a7a0
msgid "In ALTHOLD mode, the aggregate threat is translated into an attempt to add lean input into the pilot's commands to move the Copter away from the aggregate obstructions. The pilot can still overcome these additions to his command inputs and fly into a object, if determined to do so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-simple-object-avoidance.rst:36
#: 267f7f04a9164ba89947ec774504de43
msgid "In LOITER, either stopping in front of the object or a \"sliding\" algorithm is used to avoid it. \"Sliding\" involves slowing and slightly yawing as the vehicle approaches the object. For example, if Copter approaches a fence line at an angle, it will \"slide along\" the fence as the operator pushes the Copter toward the fence. Head-on approaches would stop, even if the pilot continues to \"pushes\" it forward."
msgstr ""

